First check the point map of the marked word against a balanced table, then
check thirteen iterations of that table. This shares the word evaluation
instead of expanding the full word thirteen times at every point.
All finite checks use kernel reduction. The table alone asserts nothing.

The original generator data and attribution are in
`Tits/Atlas1600ParrottData.lean`; the word uses Parrott (1972), p.683.
The tables can be regenerated by `source/generate.py` in this directory.
-/

